Detecting duplicates: the all-pairs scan is **O(n²) time, O(1) space**. Remembering what you've seen in a set flips it:

```go
func hasDup(s []int) bool {
    seen := make(map[int]struct{}, len(s)) // O(n) space
    for _, v := range s {                  // O(n) time
        if _, ok := seen[v]; ok { return true }
        seen[v] = struct{}{}
    }
    return false
}
```

Now **O(n) time, O(n) space**. The discipline interviewers reward: *always quote both axes*. The trade isn't free — 'remember everything' can blow a node's RAM at scale, which is why a sort-then-scan variant (O(n log n) time, O(1) extra space) is sometimes the right call instead.
